# SuperBikeShed v2: Technical Documentation

This directory contains the complete set of technical documentation, architectural specifications, and design documents for the SuperBikeShed v2 project.

## 1. Core Architecture

- **[Architectural Vision](Trikeshed/docs/Architectural_Vision.md)**: Outlines the high-level vision for the project, combining features from CouchDB, IPFS, and modern networking principles.
- **[Project Roadmap and Future Enhancements](Trikeshed/docs/Project_Roadmap.md)**: Details the strategic roadmap, documentation requirements, and long-term vision for future enhancements.
- **[Feature Enhancement Plan](Trikeshed/docs/Feature_Enhancement_Plan.md)**: A detailed plan for enhancing and completing the core features of the project.
- **[Platform Bus (N-Way Cache) Design](platform_bus_nway_cache_design.md)**: Describes the design of the platform bus that interconnects the various protocol and agent islands.

## 2. System Specifications

- **[Kademlia DHT Specification](Trikeshed/docs/Kademlia_DHT_Specification.md)**: Specification for the Kademlia-based Distributed Hash Table.
- **[Gossip Service Specification](Trikeshed/docs/Gossip_Service_Specification.md)**: Specification for the Gossip Distribution Service.
- **[Message Serialization Specification](Trikeshed/docs/Message_Serialization_Specification.md)**: Defines the binary message formats and serialization principles for all network communication.
- **[Security and Network Specification](Trikeshed/docs/Security_and_Network_Specification.md)**: Details the security model, including message signing, spam resistance, and NAT traversal strategies.

## 3. Component Design and Implementation

- **[LJSON Parser Design](Trikeshed/docs/LJSON_Parser_Design.md)**: A detailed breakdown of the high-performance, SIMD-accelerated JSON bitmap parser.
- **[KSP Join Processor](Trikeshed/docs/KSP_JOIN_PROCESSOR_IMPLEMENTATION.md)**: Technical design for the KSP-based processor that provides a zero-cost `Join` abstraction.
- **[IODaemon Design and Test Summary](Trikeshed/docs/IODaemon_Design_and_Test_Summary.md)**: A comprehensive summary of the high-performance Linux I/O interop system using `io_uring`.
- **[SPI NIO and Boilerplate Cleanup Summary](Trikeshed/docs/SPI_NIO_CLEANUP_SUMMARY.md)**: Summary of the Service Provider Interface (SPI) system implemented to clean up NIO boilerplate.
- **[Agent-Bus Interaction Model](Trikeshed/docs/agent_bus_interaction.md)**: Describes how agents interact with the underlying DHT and Gossip services through a unified API.

## 4. Development and Integration Guides

- **[Core Idioms and Type Abstractions](Trikeshed/docs/Core_Idioms_and_Type_Abstractions.md)**: A guide to the fundamental coding idioms and type-aliases used throughout the Trikeshed library.
- **[Component Manifest & Anti-Regression Protocol](Trikeshed/docs/ANTI_REGRESSION_PROTECTION.md)**: A manifest of critical components that are protected against accidental modification or deletion.
- **[IntelliJ Project Enumerator CLI](tools/intellij-project-enumerator/README.md)**: Documentation for the CLI tool that parses IntelliJ IDEA project files.
- **[IntelliJ Integration Guide](nexus/docs/intellij_integration_guide.md)**: Guidance on how the Nexus IntelliJ Plugin integrates with the broader Nexus system.

## 5. Project Management and Historical Documents

- **[TODO Roadmap & Project Status](todo/TODO_Roadmap.md)**: A comprehensive list of pending tasks, conceptual features, and areas for future development.
- **[RTS Game Evolution Analysis](rtsgame/EVOLUTION_ANALYSIS.md)**: A re-assimilation of the complete evolution trajectory of the RTS game project.
- **[Release Engineering Path](RELEASE_ENGINEERING_PATH.md)**: The complete automation pipeline connecting dense bitgraph processing through the entire Kotlin toolchain.
